01:01:23.600 --> 01:01:26.120
Did they relocate to Scranton?
他们搬到斯克兰顿去了吗？

1323
01:01:26.600 --> 01:01:27.740
These are good questions.
这些都是好问题。

1324
01:01:28.140 --> 01:01:32.860
Well, on the DVD commentary, BJ said that Matt Sohn did a really cool thing.
对了，在DVD评论音轨中，BJ说马特·索恩做了一件非常酷的事。

1325
01:01:33.000 --> 01:01:38.420
After everything was shot, he went back in and washed out the color of the footage of the
拍完所有内容后，他回去把电影素材的

1326
01:01:38.420 --> 01:01:42.500
movie to make it look even more distinctly different from the documentary footage.
颜色调淡，让它看起来与纪录片素材有更明显的区别。

1327
01:01:42.500 --> 01:01:43.580
And I could see it.
我能看出来。

1328
01:01:43.720 --> 01:01:46.980
I thought that was really smart because then you knew when you were watching the episode
我觉得这非常聪明，因为这样你就知道什么时候在看正片

1329
01:01:46.980 --> 01:01:49.560
versus when you were watching Threat Level Midnight.
什么时候在看《午夜威胁》。

1330
01:01:49.660 --> 01:01:49.860
Yeah.
是的。

1331
01:01:50.780 --> 01:01:53.960
Oh, one more thing from the scene that I thought was really fun.
哦，场景里还有一件事我觉得非常有趣。

1332
01:01:54.780 --> 01:01:56.660
You know, Golden Face has a golden gun.
你知道，黄金脸有一把黄金枪。

1333
01:01:56.960 --> 01:01:57.120
Yeah.
对。

1334
01:01:57.620 --> 01:02:01.120
BJ said Phil Shea just took it upon himself to make a golden gun.
BJ说菲尔·谢伊自作主张做了一把黄金枪。

1335
01:02:01.120 --> 01:02:02.580
It was not scripted that way.
剧本里并没有这样写。

1336
01:02:02.740 --> 01:02:03.680
Oh, it was perfect.
哦，太完美了。

1337
01:02:03.680 --> 01:02:04.280
I know.
我知道。

1338
01:02:04.360 --> 01:02:09.580
And BJ was so tickled when he got to the ice rink and he saw the gold gun for Golden
当BJ到达滑冰场看到黄金脸的黄金枪时，他高兴坏了。

1339
01:02:09.580 --> 01:02:09.920
Face.
面。

1340
01:02:10.220 --> 01:02:15.500
But this is just the example of how every department was so excited to be a part of this project.
但这正是一个例子，说明了每个部门都为能参与这个项目而兴奋不已。

1341
01:02:15.680 --> 01:02:16.360
It's so true.
确实如此。

1342
01:02:17.080 --> 01:02:20.720
Scranton is going to realize that he's got to take out the guy who won.
斯克兰顿会意识到他必须除掉那个获胜的家伙。

1343
01:02:21.080 --> 01:02:22.500
Well, he was number two.
嗯，他当时是第二名。

1344
01:02:22.500 --> 01:02:25.640
So if number one is gone, he'll get the slot.
所以如果第一名不在了，他就能顶替这个位置。

1345
01:02:25.840 --> 01:02:26.400
That's right.
没错。

1346
01:02:26.640 --> 01:02:28.760
So he strangles Oscar's character.
于是他掐死了奥斯卡的角色。

1347
01:02:28.960 --> 01:02:30.140
With an American flag.
用一面美国国旗。

1348
01:02:30.140 --> 01:02:31.520
Yeah, he apologizes.
对，他道了歉。

1349
01:02:32.260 --> 01:02:35.680
This scene is much longer in the DVD version.
DVD版本的这个场景要长得多。

1350
01:02:35.820 --> 01:02:37.000
So much longer.
长得多。

1351
01:02:37.360 --> 01:02:44.100
Oscar really makes a meal out of, like, his, like, legs kicking and all of it.
奥斯卡真的把那场戏演得太夸张了，比如他的双腿乱踢什么的。

1352
01:02:44.260 --> 01:02:45.100
It's pretty hilarious.
简直笑死人了。

1353
01:02:45.360 --> 01:02:50.520
One of my favorite details is that after Oscar has died, he continues to blink.
我最喜欢的细节之一就是，奥斯卡死后还在不停地眨眼。

1354
01:02:50.680 --> 01:02:50.800
Yeah.
对啊。

1355
01:02:51.060 --> 01:02:51.600
Did you notice?
你注意到了吗？

1356
01:02:51.700 --> 01:02:52.440
Oh, I noticed.
哦，我注意到了。

1357
01:02:52.740 --> 01:02:56.800
This death scene is making everyone in the conference room a little uncomfortable.
这场死亡戏让会议室里的每个人都觉得有点不自在。

1358
01:02:57.100 --> 01:02:57.740
They're like, wow.
他们大概在想，哇。

1359
01:02:57.960 --> 01:02:58.880
That was dark.
这也太黑暗了。

1360
01:02:59.140 --> 01:02:59.460
Yeah.
就是说啊。

1361
01:02:59.460 --> 01:03:02.340
Well, you have to believe that they watched the extended cut.
好吧，你得相信他们看的是加长版。

1362
01:03:02.680 --> 01:03:02.960
Yes.
没错。

1363
01:03:05.420 --> 01:03:09.060
Back at Scarn Manor, Samuel is going to reveal some information.
回到斯卡恩庄园，塞缪尔要透露一些信息。

1364
01:03:09.060 --> 01:03:14.960
He has intercepted a name, Jasmine Winsong, but he doesn't know who the Funky Cat is.
他截获了一个名字，茉莉·温松，但他不知道“时髦猫”是谁。

1365
01:03:15.180 --> 01:03:17.320
And Scarn says, not who, what?
然后斯卡恩说，不是谁，是什么？

1366
01:03:17.520 --> 01:03:20.800
Because the Funky Cat is the hippest jazz club in town.
因为“时髦猫”是镇上最时髦的爵士乐俱乐部。

1367
01:03:21.340 --> 01:03:27.080
Well, lady, before we go to the Funky Cat, I think we should take a little break.
好吧，女士，在我们去“时髦猫”之前，我想我们应该休息一会儿。

1368
01:03:27.240 --> 01:03:27.440
Yeah.
好啊。

1369
01:03:28.280 --> 01:03:28.700
Because.
因为。

1370
01:03:29.020 --> 01:03:30.660
You're going to put your boob back in your bra?
你要把胸部塞回文胸里吗？

1371
01:03:30.840 --> 01:03:38.280
I actually am going to go and see if maybe I do some adjustments, if I can make some more room on the left side.
我其实是要去看看能不能调整一下，好给左边腾出更多空间。

1372
01:03:38.700 --> 01:03:39.560
I'll let you know.
我随时告诉你。

1373
01:03:39.660 --> 01:03:44.240
When we come back, Jenna's boob will be in place, and we're going to meet Jasmine Winsong.
等我们回来，珍娜的胸部就会归位，然后我们要去见茉莉·温松。

1374
01:03:44.240 --> 01:03:44.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1375
01:03:53.280 --> 01:03:54.180
We're back.
我们回来了。

1376
01:03:54.520 --> 01:03:55.860
Here's what I've discovered.
这是我发现的情况。

1377
01:03:56.220 --> 01:03:56.420
Okay.
好吧。

1378
01:03:57.020 --> 01:04:03.500
My boob is in, but it doesn't feel in because there's cup and then there's a little lace.
我的胸是进去了，但感觉没进去，因为有罩杯，然后还有一点蕾丝。

1379
01:04:03.920 --> 01:04:04.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1380
01:04:04.380 --> 01:04:07.420
And I'm feeling it kind of bulge on the lace.
我感觉它在蕾丝那里有点鼓出来。

1381
01:04:07.660 --> 01:04:07.980
Okay.
好吧。

1382
01:04:08.420 --> 01:04:09.400
So it's in.
所以它进去了。

1383
01:04:09.740 --> 01:04:10.100
Yeah.
对。

1384
01:04:10.380 --> 01:04:11.600
It's going to be fine.
会没事的。

1385
01:04:11.700 --> 01:04:12.680
But it doesn't want to be there.
但它就是不想呆在那儿。

1386
01:04:13.020 --> 01:04:15.160
You know, I was trying to level up, Angela.
你知道的，安吉拉，我当时想升级一下。

1387
01:04:15.160 --> 01:04:15.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1388
01:04:15.440 --> 01:04:17.060
I was trying to maybe.
我当时想也许。

1389
01:04:17.440 --> 01:04:19.120
Give the undergarments a zhuzh.
给内衣弄点时髦的修饰。

1390
01:04:19.300 --> 01:04:19.740
Yes.
是的。

1391
01:04:19.920 --> 01:04:20.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1392
01:04:20.020 --> 01:04:22.920
And so I went with a bra with some lace on it.
所以我选了一款带蕾丝的文胸。

1393
01:04:23.140 --> 01:04:23.420
Yeah.
对。

1394
01:04:23.900 --> 01:04:25.900
And I don't think the lace is for me.
而且我觉得蕾丝不适合我。

1395
01:04:26.180 --> 01:04:29.960
I just, you know, I'm almost 50, and I think I know what I like.
我只是，你知道的，我快50岁了，我想我知道自己喜欢什么。

1396
01:04:30.020 --> 01:04:30.620
I disagree.
我不同意。

1397
01:04:30.620 --> 01:04:32.400
I think you can wear a lace in your 50s.
我觉得你50多岁也可以穿蕾丝。

1398
01:04:32.400 --> 01:04:34.900
I'm not saying you can't wear lace in your 50s.
我不是说你50多岁不能穿蕾丝。

1399
01:04:34.900 --> 01:04:37.760
I'm saying my left boob is not a lace fan.
我是说我的左胸不喜欢蕾丝。

1400
01:04:38.020 --> 01:04:40.440
I think your left boob is a lace fan.
我觉得你的左胸挺喜欢蕾丝的。

1401
01:04:40.440 --> 01:04:44.680
I just think the lace is a little wimpy, and you might need some stronger lace.
我只是觉得这蕾丝有点太单薄了，你可能需要更扎实的蕾丝。

1402
01:04:45.420 --> 01:04:45.940
Oh.
哦。

1403
01:04:46.780 --> 01:04:49.760
You need big boob lace.
你需要大胸专属蕾丝。

1404
01:04:50.220 --> 01:04:50.620
Oh.
哦。

1405
01:04:51.040 --> 01:04:53.220
Maybe right now you have medium boob lace.
也许你现在用的是中号胸部蕾丝。

1406
01:04:53.400 --> 01:04:54.140
I don't know.
我不知道。

1407
01:04:54.540 --> 01:04:56.540
Well, you know who's probably wearing some lace?
好吧，你知道谁可能穿着蕾丝吗？

1408
01:04:56.780 --> 01:04:57.880
Jasmine Winsong.
茉莉·温松。

1409
01:04:57.960 --> 01:04:59.660
How do you like that for a transition?
你觉得这个转折怎么样？

1410
01:04:59.960 --> 01:05:01.300
I think you did that great.
我觉得你转得太棒了。

1411
01:05:02.100 --> 01:05:03.540
She's up on the piano.
她站在钢琴上。

1412
01:05:04.440 --> 01:05:08.080
She's singing as Michael enters the funky cat.
当迈克尔走进这个时髦的家伙时，她在唱歌。

1413
01:05:08.240 --> 01:05:08.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1414
01:05:09.280 --> 01:05:11.760
And Michael Skarn sits down at the piano.
然后迈克尔·斯卡恩在钢琴前坐下。

1415
01:05:12.420 --> 01:05:16.860
We cut to this amazing Jan talking head that I just simply could not love more.
我们切到一个精彩的简的单人访谈镜头，我简直不能更爱了。

1416
01:05:17.140 --> 01:05:18.920
It was so perfect.
简直完美。

1417
01:05:18.920 --> 01:05:23.140
I had to go to the shooting draft because I had to know if the bit she was doing...
我不得不去查拍摄剧本，因为我必须知道她刚才演的那段……

1418
01:05:23.140 --> 01:05:24.840
Where she couldn't open the car door?
就是她打不开车门的那段？

1419
01:05:25.020 --> 01:05:25.280
Yes.
对。

1420
01:05:25.280 --> 01:05:26.920
I had to know if that was scripted.
我得知道那是不是剧本里写的。

1421
01:05:26.920 --> 01:05:27.700
Was it scripted?
是剧本写的吗？

1422
01:05:27.780 --> 01:05:28.260
No.
不是。

1423
01:05:28.260 --> 01:05:29.400
It's so great.
太棒了。

1424
01:05:29.640 --> 01:05:31.040
It's not in the script.
剧本里没有。

1425
01:05:31.480 --> 01:05:33.720
This is all it says in the shooting draft.
拍摄剧本里只写了这些。

1426
01:05:34.200 --> 01:05:35.220
Jan talking head.
简的单人访谈镜头。

1427
01:05:35.360 --> 01:05:37.180
She's on the street walking to her car.
她在街上走向她的车。

1428
01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:39.620
Jan says, he finished his movie?
简说，他拍完他的电影了？

1429
01:05:39.820 --> 01:05:40.300
No kidding.
不是吧。

1430
01:05:40.640 --> 01:05:41.100
Wow.
哇。

1431
01:05:41.300 --> 01:05:41.820
That's great.
那太棒了。

1432
01:05:42.100 --> 01:05:42.680
Good for him.
真为他高兴。

1433
01:05:43.020 --> 01:05:44.960
And I heard he has a serious girlfriend.
我听说他有个认真的女朋友。

1434
01:05:45.200 --> 01:05:46.100
That's so great.
那真是太棒了。

1435
01:05:46.240 --> 01:05:47.040
I'm great too.
我也过得很好。

1436
01:05:47.980 --> 01:05:48.480
Okay.
好吧。

1437
01:05:48.700 --> 01:05:50.340
Well, sadly, they cut out the end.
唉，可惜他们把结尾剪掉了。

1438
01:05:50.500 --> 01:05:50.800
Yeah.
是啊。

1439
01:05:50.800 --> 01:05:52.900
Because I would have loved that snark from Jan.
因为我超想看简那种讽刺劲儿的。

1440
01:05:53.080 --> 01:05:53.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1441
01:05:53.800 --> 01:05:58.180
I love the choice that she's carrying a bag of dry cleaning to her car.
我特别喜欢她提着一袋干洗衣物走向汽车这个设定。

1442
01:05:58.380 --> 01:06:00.560
I love that she can't get the door open.
我喜欢她打不开车门的样子。

1443
01:06:00.820 --> 01:06:07.060
I love that they've clearly ambushed her on the street to ask her about her role in Threat Level Midnight.
我喜欢他们显然是在街上突袭采访她，问她关于在《午夜威胁》里的角色。

1444
01:06:07.300 --> 01:06:08.120
I love it all.
我全都爱。

1445
01:06:08.280 --> 01:06:09.200
I love her performance.
我爱她的表演。

1446
01:06:09.620 --> 01:06:17.700
And by the way, Jasmine Winsong is a very important part of this movie because she is going to sing backwards a very important clue.
顺便说一句，茉莉·温松在这部电影中扮演着非常重要的角色，因为她将倒着唱出一个极其重要的线索。

1447
01:06:17.700 --> 01:06:23.840
Yes, Michael is going to record it with a special mini tape recorder that has like a little label maker that says backwards.
对，迈克尔会用一个特殊的迷你录音机录下来，上面还贴了个写着“倒放”的小标签机标签。

1448
01:06:24.220 --> 01:06:29.120
Because if you put a label that says backwards, it just plays things backwards for you.
因为只要你贴上一个写着“倒放”的标签，它就会自动为你倒着播放。

1449
01:06:29.420 --> 01:06:33.200
The message says the hostages are under the stadium.
信息说人质在体育场下面。

1450
01:06:33.520 --> 01:06:38.140
But as soon as she delivers that message, she gets a dart to the neck.
但她刚传达完这个信息，脖子上就中了一记飞镖。

1451
01:06:38.320 --> 01:06:39.980
By assassin Troy.
死神特洛伊。

1452
01:06:40.480 --> 01:06:41.000
Yes.
是的。

1453
01:06:41.360 --> 01:06:43.060
Troy Underbridge is back.
特洛伊·昂德布里奇回来了。

1454
01:06:43.400 --> 01:06:46.680
And you know, his role is even larger in the extended version.
而且你知道，在加长版中他的戏份更多了。

1455
01:06:46.980 --> 01:06:47.200
Yeah.
没错。

1456
01:06:47.840 --> 01:06:48.680
Location alert.
地点提醒。

1457
01:06:48.820 --> 01:06:54.780
The Funky Cat Jazz Club was filmed at Stove Piper Lounge in Northridge, California.
时髦猫爵士俱乐部是在加州诺斯里奇的火炉管休息室拍摄的。

1458
01:06:55.040 --> 01:06:59.340
And the lyrics for the song, They Call Me Jasmine Winsong, were written by B.J.
歌曲《他们叫我茉莉·温松》的歌词是由B.J.

1459
01:06:59.480 --> 01:06:59.920
Novak.
诺瓦克写的。

1460
01:07:00.020 --> 01:07:04.920
And the music was written by Eve Nelson, who was our amazing go-to composer on our show.
音乐则是由伊芙·尼尔森创作的，她是我们在节目中御用且了不起的作曲家。

1461
01:07:05.180 --> 01:07:09.900
Back at the stadium, our hostage, Sandra, played by Pam.
回到体育场，由帕姆饰演的人质桑德拉。

1462
01:07:10.060 --> 01:07:10.420
Yes.
对。

1463
01:07:10.660 --> 01:07:13.320
Is going to beg Golden Face to let them all go.
正请求黄金脸放所有人走。

1464
01:07:13.520 --> 01:07:14.860
But it doesn't work.
但无济于事。

1465
01:07:15.060 --> 01:07:15.500
No.
没有。

1466
01:07:15.500 --> 01:07:18.700
In fact, he decides to take out a hostage.
事实上，他决定干掉一个人质。

1467
01:07:19.080 --> 01:07:19.560
Toby.
托比。

1468
01:07:19.860 --> 01:07:22.320
Yeah, he needs to show how serious he is.
对，他需要表现出他有多认真。

1469
01:07:22.580 --> 01:07:24.660
We had a fan question from Anna T.
我们收到了来自伊利诺伊州皮奥里亚的

1470
01:07:24.820 --> 01:07:25.700
in Peoria, Illinois.
安娜·T.的粉丝提问。

1471
01:07:25.700 --> 01:07:32.520
In this episode, Michael says that the scene with Toby's head explosion was the most expensive
在这集里，迈克尔说托比头部爆炸的那场戏是电影里所有场景中

1472
01:07:32.520 --> 01:07:34.260
among all the scenes in the movie.
最贵的一场。

1473
01:07:34.620 --> 01:07:40.160
And I'm wondering, which scene was the most expensive that you shot in the whole series
我想知道，在《办公室》整部剧里你拍摄的最贵的场景是哪一个，

1474
01:07:40.160 --> 01:07:44.400
of The Office, and which one was the most expensive for this episode?
而这一集里最贵的又是哪一个？

1475
01:07:44.400 --> 01:07:49.860
Well, as far as being the most expensive in the whole series, I have a guess.
嗯，就整部剧最贵的场景而言，我有个猜测。

1476
01:07:50.180 --> 01:07:50.660
Yes.
好。

1477
01:07:50.880 --> 01:07:54.120
I know they had to build a whole entire gas station and a freeway.
我知道他们不得不建造一整座加油站和一条高速公路。

1478
01:07:54.500 --> 01:07:54.980
Yes.
没错。

1479
01:07:55.220 --> 01:07:56.220
You're right, Angela.
你说得对，安吉拉。

1480
01:07:56.760 --> 01:07:58.740
The Jim Pam proposal scene.
吉姆和帕姆的求婚场景。

1481
01:07:59.160 --> 01:08:06.180
He said the second most expensive would probably go to filming on the boat in Niagara Falls, especially
他说第二贵的可能是在尼亚加拉瀑布的船上拍摄，尤其是

1482
01:08:06.180 --> 01:08:09.520
if you include all the travel and location expenses to get there.
如果你算上到达那里的所有差旅和外景费用的话。

1483
01:08:09.840 --> 01:08:14.380
And Anna, as far as the most expensive scene in the episode, on the commentary, you said,
安娜，至于这一集中最贵的场景，在评论音轨里你说过，

1484
01:08:14.400 --> 01:08:19.680
BJ said definitely he thought it was the Toby explosion, but Randy said, that's not accurate.
BJ说他绝对认为是托比爆炸那场，但兰迪说，那并不准确。

1485
01:08:20.080 --> 01:08:20.800
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

1486
01:08:21.020 --> 01:08:21.420
Really.
真的。

1487
01:08:21.940 --> 01:08:28.040
Randy thinks the sequence of scenes at the Funky Cat bar were more expensive because it included
兰迪认为时髦猫酒吧的一系列场景更贵，因为它们包含了

1488
01:08:28.040 --> 01:08:32.460
all of these elements, the music, the choreography, the extras, the costumes, the set dressing,
所有这些元素：音乐、编舞、群众演员、服装、布景道具、

1489
01:08:32.800 --> 01:08:35.620
all the signage, the locations, and the guest stars.
所有的标牌、外景以及客串明星。

1490
01:08:36.100 --> 01:08:36.860
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1491
01:08:36.900 --> 01:08:37.760
That makes sense.
这倒也是。

1492
01:08:37.960 --> 01:08:38.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1493
01:08:38.420 --> 01:08:40.960
So Funky Cat wins most expensive scene.
所以时髦猫赢得了最贵场景的称号。

1494
01:08:41.220 --> 01:08:43.560
We got another fan question from Hannah B.
我们收到了来自威斯康星州的

1495
01:08:43.660 --> 01:08:44.100
in Wisconsin.
汉娜·B.的另一个粉丝提问。

1496
01:08:44.400 --> 01:08:48.120
I would love to know how you did make Toby's head explode.
我很想知道你们是怎么让托比的头爆炸的。

1497
01:08:48.380 --> 01:08:52.580
How many times were you able to get this shot, and did you have a safety meeting?
这个镜头你们拍了几次，还有你们开过安全会议吗？

1498
01:08:52.960 --> 01:08:59.280
Well, Hannah, BJ said they made two Toby heads, and in order to make the heads, Paul had to
嗯，汉娜，BJ说他们做了两个托比的头部模型，为了制作这些模型，保罗不得不

1499
01:08:59.280 --> 01:09:03.400
sit in a full-face plaster mold for hours.
在全脸石膏模具里坐上好几个小时。

1500
01:09:03.960 --> 01:09:05.040
Hours of time.
花了好几个小时。

1501
01:09:05.200 --> 01:09:09.400
BJ said he could have been producing our show, but instead he was just sitting in a face mold.
BJ说他本可以制作我们的节目，但他却只是坐在一个脸模里。

1502
01:09:09.940 --> 01:09:14.260
After that was done, to get this shot, they rigged each of the molds with mild explosives.
那之后为了拍这个镜头，他们在每个模具里都装了微型炸药。

1503
01:09:14.660 --> 01:09:19.780
They filled one of them with blood, and then they set up cameras from three different
他们在其中一个里面灌满了血，然后从三个不同的

1504
01:09:19.780 --> 01:09:22.880
angles, and they filmed them exploding in slow motion.
角度架设了摄像机，拍下了它们慢动作爆炸的画面。

1505
01:09:23.600 --> 01:09:27.600
When they went back to review the footage, they said the one that was filled with blood
等他们回去查看素材时，他们说那个灌了血的

1506
01:09:27.600 --> 01:09:29.220
was just too disturbing.
实在太让人不安了。

1507
01:09:29.740 --> 01:09:30.660
Oh, I bet.
哦，我敢说肯定是。

1508
01:09:31.160 --> 01:09:32.440
It was just too gruesome.
实在是太血腥了。

1509
01:09:32.600 --> 01:09:34.340
It needed to look super fakey.
它得看起来超级假才行。

1510
01:09:34.340 --> 01:09:34.980
It did.
确实如此。

1511
01:09:35.140 --> 01:09:38.160
So that's why they ended up using the one that they did.
所以这就是为什么他们最后用了现在这个版本。

1512
01:09:38.440 --> 01:09:42.860
I do remember Paul talking about sitting in all that plaster, though, and he said it was
不过我确实记得保罗说过他坐在那些石膏里，

1513
01:09:42.860 --> 01:09:44.300
a miserable experience.
那真是一段痛苦的经历。

1514
01:09:44.640 --> 01:09:46.740
I mean, claustrophobic.
我是说，幽闭恐惧症。

1515
01:09:46.880 --> 01:09:47.040
Yes.
是的。

1516
01:09:47.040 --> 01:09:47.660
Like, for hours.
就像是，持续好几个小时。

1517
01:09:47.920 --> 01:09:50.960
Like, don't you have, like, a little tiny straw you breathe through?
就像，你们难道没有那种用来呼吸的超级细的小吸管吗？

1518
01:09:51.120 --> 01:09:51.400
Yeah.
对。

1519
01:09:51.680 --> 01:09:51.940
Ugh.
呃。

1520
01:09:52.560 --> 01:09:56.420
Randy confirmed that, yes, we definitely had a safety meeting.
兰迪证实了，没错，我们绝对开过安全会议。

1521
01:09:56.620 --> 01:09:57.240
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1522
01:09:57.240 --> 01:10:05.900
We had to discuss protecting the camera crew from the shards of Toby's plaster flying, yes,
我们得讨论怎么保护摄影组免受托比飞溅的石膏碎片伤害，没错，

1523
01:10:06.120 --> 01:10:06.400
everywhere.
到处都是。

1524
01:10:06.700 --> 01:10:10.500
But we removed the cast from the shot, which you can tell, which is very funny.
但我们把演员从镜头里移开了，一眼就能看出来，这非常搞笑。

1525
01:10:10.680 --> 01:10:12.800
No one is sitting around the dummy Toby.
没有人在假托比周围坐着。

1526
01:10:13.080 --> 01:10:18.140
And the whole thing cost about $5,700 in special effects and labor.
整个特效和人工成本大约是5700美元。

1527
01:10:19.160 --> 01:10:23.140
Skarna and Samuel are going to arrive to save the hostages.
斯卡纳和塞缪尔要来拯救人质了。

1528
01:10:23.420 --> 01:10:24.600
It's very exciting.
太激动人心了。

1529
01:10:24.820 --> 01:10:25.300
I know.
我知道。

1530
01:10:25.300 --> 01:10:30.600
And for some reason, Golden Face is going to reveal where the bomb is hidden.
而且出于某种原因，黄金脸要透露炸弹藏在哪里了。

1531
01:10:30.820 --> 01:10:32.040
It's in the puck.
在冰球里。

1532
01:10:32.500 --> 01:10:32.960
Yeah.
对。

1533
01:10:33.240 --> 01:10:39.580
He tosses it to Skarn, and Skarn holds it and starts to reminisce about his life with his
他把冰球扔给斯卡恩，斯卡恩接着冰球，开始回忆他和妻子的生活。

1534
01:10:39.580 --> 01:10:39.900
wife.
妻子。

1535
01:10:40.160 --> 01:10:43.280
There's like a little montage playing on the hockey puck.
冰球上好像在播放一小段蒙太奇。

1536
01:10:43.640 --> 01:10:46.020
This was our director, Tucker Gates, his idea.
这是我们的导演塔克·盖茨的主意。

1537
01:10:46.340 --> 01:10:49.740
And in the flashback montage, here's what Skarn sees.
在闪回蒙太奇里，斯卡恩看到了这些。

1538
01:10:50.060 --> 01:10:55.280
He sees himself painting his wife's toenails, and he's kind of blowing on them to dry them.
他看到自己给妻子涂脚趾甲油，还一边吹气想弄干它们。

1539
01:10:55.880 --> 01:11:04.620
He's also walking maybe animal cookie crackers or some kind of cracker across a woman's belly
他还拿着动物饼干之类的饼干在一个女人的肚子上

1540
01:11:04.620 --> 01:11:05.880
while they're laying on the grass.
走来走去，当时他们正躺在草地上。

1541
01:11:06.100 --> 01:11:08.040
And then a catch-up fight.
然后是番茄酱大战。

1542
01:11:08.460 --> 01:11:15.660
This montage makes so obvious how Michael has never really been in a healthy relationship.
这个蒙太奇把迈克尔从未经历过健康的恋爱关系这一点表现得淋漓尽致。

1543
01:11:15.660 --> 01:11:25.060
Because when he had to create a flashback love montage, these were the ideas he had of a
因为当他必须创作一段闪回的爱情蒙太奇时，这就是他对一段

1544
01:11:25.060 --> 01:11:26.320
blissful relationship.
幸福关系的想法。

1545
01:11:26.780 --> 01:11:29.380
But I mean, Angela, catch-up fight.
但我的意思是，安吉拉，番茄酱大战。

1546
01:11:29.560 --> 01:11:31.240
We've all done that, right?
我们都做过这个，对吧？

1547
01:11:31.240 --> 01:11:32.060
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1548
01:11:32.280 --> 01:11:34.720
That's totally a normal part of courtship.
这绝对是求爱过程中的正常部分。

1549
01:11:34.880 --> 01:11:40.860
And I personally love when Lee and I are in bed, and he moves an animal cracker across
我个人非常喜欢我和李躺在床上时，他在我肚子上

1550
01:11:40.860 --> 01:11:41.440
my belly.
移动一块动物饼干。

1551
01:11:42.020 --> 01:11:43.140
Well, I'm like-
嗯，我当时就——

1552
01:11:43.140 --> 01:11:43.340
It's hot.
好热啊。

1553
01:11:43.340 --> 01:11:44.560
I'm like, hey, what?
我心想，嘿，怎么了？

1554
01:11:44.700 --> 01:11:45.720
You want to paint my toenails?
你想帮我涂脚趾甲油吗？

1555
01:11:46.140 --> 01:11:48.520
I mean, only if you blow on him after.
我的意思是，除非你事后帮他吹一吹。

1556
01:11:49.440 --> 01:11:53.580
Well, Skarn is going to hurl the puck right back at Golden Face, and he's going to yell,
嗯，斯卡恩要把冰球直接扔回给黄金脸，然后他会大喊，

1557
01:11:53.780 --> 01:11:54.660
go puck yourself.
去你妈的冰球。

1558
01:11:55.160 --> 01:11:57.480
Charlie Grandy shared that he wrote, go puck yourself.
查理·格兰迪分享说，那句去你妈的冰球是他写的。

1559
01:11:57.480 --> 01:11:58.160
Nice.
不错。

1560
01:11:59.060 --> 01:12:01.600
This whole thing is going to end terribly.
整件事最后一定会糟糕透顶。

1561
01:12:02.380 --> 01:12:08.060
Golden Face is going to try to shoot Michael Skarn, and Samuel is going to jump in and take
黄金脸要开枪射击迈克尔·斯卡恩，然后塞缪尔会冲过去挡下

1562
01:12:08.060 --> 01:12:08.660
that bullet.
那一枪。

1563
01:12:09.420 --> 01:12:12.260
And then Golden Face is going to shoot Michael Skarn right after.
然后黄金脸紧接着就会枪击迈克尔·斯卡恩。

1564
01:12:12.760 --> 01:12:15.660
Apparently, Samuel diving in front of the bullet was not scripted.
显然，塞缪尔飞身扑向子弹并不是剧本里写的。

1565
01:12:15.680 --> 01:12:16.300
It was not scripted.
这不是剧本安排的。

1566
01:12:16.320 --> 01:12:17.220
That was just Dwight.
那是德怀特临场发挥的。

1567
01:12:18.220 --> 01:12:25.180
That one bullet pierced Michael Skarn's brain, lungs, heart, back, and balls.
那一颗子弹穿透了迈克尔·斯卡恩的大脑、肺部、心脏、背部和蛋蛋。

1568
01:12:25.500 --> 01:12:27.320
But it's going to take a lot more than that.
但想要打倒斯卡恩

1569
01:12:27.480 --> 01:12:28.540
To take Skarn down.
可没那么容易。

1570
01:12:28.960 --> 01:12:33.060
Good thing he's got a big, busty nurse to help make everything feel better.
幸好他有一个身材火辣的大胸护士来帮忙抚慰一切。

1571
01:12:33.240 --> 01:12:34.200
Oh, Helene.
哦，海伦。

1572
01:12:34.460 --> 01:12:36.880
How awkward could you imagine?
你能想象有多尴尬吗？

1573
01:12:37.340 --> 01:12:44.060
I mean, Pam is trying so hard to be supportive of this movie.
我是说，帕姆为了支持这部电影已经尽力了。

1574
01:12:44.220 --> 01:12:49.760
And clearly, clearly, she never knew that her mom filmed a scene for Threat Level Midnight.
而且很显然，她以前根本不知道她妈妈为《危情时刻：午夜》拍过一场戏。

1575
01:12:49.900 --> 01:12:51.940
I feel like she's discovering it in the moment.
我觉得她是在这时候才发现的。

1576
01:12:52.100 --> 01:12:53.960
I can't believe her mom wouldn't tell her.
真不敢相信她妈妈竟然没告诉她。

1577
01:12:53.960 --> 01:12:58.720
I wore a super-kadooper push-up bra and leaned into the camera.
我穿了超级无敌聚拢文胸，还把身子探向了镜头。

1578
01:12:59.280 --> 01:13:05.140
Back at the White House, a fully-recovered Skarn is going to tell the president that the bomb is in the puck.
回到白宫，完全康复的斯卡恩要告诉总统炸弹就在冰球里。

1579
01:13:05.880 --> 01:13:07.380
Plot twist coming.
剧情大反转要来了。

1580
01:13:07.820 --> 01:13:08.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1581
01:13:09.080 --> 01:13:14.360
Golden Face and his sidekick are going to walk into the president's office.
黄金脸和他的助手要走进总统办公室了。

1582
01:13:14.600 --> 01:13:15.780
They're in cahoots.
他们是一伙的。

1583
01:13:15.960 --> 01:13:16.820
With machine guns.
拿着机枪。

1584
01:13:17.080 --> 01:13:17.320
Yeah.
对。

1585
01:13:17.320 --> 01:13:19.280
The president is in on it.
总统也是同谋。

1586
01:13:19.740 --> 01:13:24.540
Skarn is going to smash a picture of Abraham Lincoln over the president's head to escape.
斯卡恩要用一张亚伯拉罕·林肯的照片砸向总统的头来逃跑。

1587
01:13:25.400 --> 01:13:29.540
Carrie Kemper pitched the joke of Michael smashing the painting over the president's head.
凯莉·肯珀提出了迈克尔用画砸总统头的这个笑话梗。

1588
01:13:29.540 --> 01:13:33.080
Well, Randy said that that picture was a public domain image.
嗯，兰迪说那张照片是公版图片。

1589
01:13:33.080 --> 01:13:34.340
It was free to use.
可以免费使用。

1590
01:13:34.480 --> 01:13:39.480
And our art department printed multiple copies of it on easy-to-tear paper.
而且我们的美术部门用易碎纸打印了好几份。

1591
01:13:40.060 --> 01:13:50.880
I love the choice that Craig made as the president in this movie to sort of stick his head out in anticipation of getting the Abraham Lincoln portrait on his head.
我特别喜欢克雷格在这部电影里演总统时做出的一个选择，就是为了迎接亚伯拉罕·林肯的肖像砸在头上，他提前把头伸了出去。

1592
01:13:51.100 --> 01:13:51.300
Yeah.
对。

1593
01:13:51.860 --> 01:13:53.220
It's so good.
太棒了。

1594
01:13:53.420 --> 01:13:53.920
It's so good.
真是太棒了。

1595
01:13:53.920 --> 01:13:59.460
I also love whenever Andy's character, Billy the bartender, is in a scene, when it cuts to Andy, he's mouthing the words.
我还喜欢只要安迪的角色，酒保比利出现在镜头里时，每当切到安迪的画面，他都在跟着对口型。

1596
01:13:59.680 --> 01:14:00.200
Yes!
没错！

1597
01:14:00.420 --> 01:14:01.320
In the conference room.
在会议室里。

1598
01:14:01.400 --> 01:14:01.560
Yeah.
对。

1599
01:14:02.080 --> 01:14:04.260
So we had a fan question from Tom M.
所以我们收到了来自密歇根州大急流城的汤姆·M.

1600
01:14:04.420 --> 01:14:06.260
in Grand Rapids, Michigan, who said,
的一个粉丝提问，他说

1601
01:14:06.420 --> 01:14:16.980
I imagine this was a tricky episode to film since you have to act in this movie how your character would act, and none of the characters are professional actors,
我想这一集拍起来挺不容易的，因为你得在这部电影里按照你角色的方式去演，而这些角色都不是专业演员，

1602
01:14:17.320 --> 01:14:18.820
except for maybe Andy.
除了安迪可能算吧。

1603
01:14:18.820 --> 01:14:23.180
How hard was it, as an actor, to act poorly?
作为一名演员，去演得很烂有多难？

1604
01:14:23.560 --> 01:14:26.520
Were there takes where maybe your acting was too good?
有没有哪几条镜头，可能你的演技太好了？

1605
01:14:27.060 --> 01:14:34.100
Tom, this is really interesting because we did all put a lot of thought into what kind of performers were each of our characters.
汤姆，这真的很有意思，因为我们确实都花了很多心思去琢磨我们各自的角色都是什么样的表演者。

1606
01:14:34.660 --> 01:14:44.440
And again, kind of like what BJ said about how Paul didn't want the camera work to be terrible, we were also directed to not be awful actors.
而且话说回来，就像BJ之前说的，保罗不希望摄像像拍得烂七八糟一样，我们也得到了指示，不能演得太糟糕。

1607
01:14:44.440 --> 01:14:49.080
Maybe a little stiff, maybe camera-aware.
也许稍微生硬一点，也许对着镜头有点不自在。

1608
01:14:49.340 --> 01:14:49.740
Yes.
对。

1609
01:14:49.760 --> 01:14:49.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1610
01:14:50.220 --> 01:14:56.380
But you've seen those videos that people post, maybe where they're acting out a skit at their job.
但你看过人们发布的那种视频吗，也许是他们在工作时演一出小品。

1611
01:14:56.580 --> 01:15:00.900
I watched some of those on YouTube because I was like, I think that would be Pam.
我在YouTube上看过一些这样的视频，因为我想，我觉得那就会是帕姆。

1612
01:15:01.180 --> 01:15:07.980
Like, Pam would just say all of her lines very simply with earnestness, almost as if she was reading them.
就像，帕姆会非常简单、极其认真地念完她所有的台词，几乎就像是在照本宣科一样。

1613
01:15:08.180 --> 01:15:08.560
Yeah.
对。

1614
01:15:09.100 --> 01:15:10.300
Without any pauses.
没有任何停顿。

1615
01:15:10.520 --> 01:15:11.380
Yes, exactly.
对，没错。

1616
01:15:11.600 --> 01:15:12.820
Without any inflections.
没有任何语调起伏。

1617
01:15:12.820 --> 01:15:20.280
Well, we're not at this part yet, but I can tell you when I had to learn the dance, I had to take the hip sass down a notch.
好吧，我们还没到这一段，但我可以告诉你，当我必须学那支舞时，我不得不把胯部的扭动收敛一点。

1618
01:15:20.440 --> 01:15:22.700
Oh, because of your natural hip sass?
哦，因为你天生胯部就很扭吗？

1619
01:15:22.720 --> 01:15:26.240
I liked to, you know, sashay, and I had to tone that down.
我喜欢，你知道的，扭捏作态，而我不得不收敛一下。

1620
01:15:26.740 --> 01:15:30.680
We are finally going to make it to the bar, and we see Billy played by Andy.
我们终于到了酒吧，然后我们看到了由安迪饰演的比利。

1621
01:15:30.860 --> 01:15:33.480
Oh, Andy was so excited to make this character happen.
哦，安迪为了把这个角色演活，可兴奋了。

1622
01:15:34.040 --> 01:15:35.360
Billy's TV doesn't work.
比利的电视坏了。

1623
01:15:35.500 --> 01:15:36.560
How's that for problems?
这算什么烦恼？

1624
01:15:36.760 --> 01:15:39.340
And I loved it when Michael's like, don't ever change, Billy.
我特别喜欢迈克尔说“千万别变，比利”的时候。

1625
01:15:41.840 --> 01:15:51.160
At 12 minutes, 52 seconds, when the group of bachelorettes give Michael a drink, did anyone else think it looked like my husband's, the F train to Brooklyn extra bitters?
在12分52秒，当单身女郎团给迈克尔一杯饮料时，有没有人觉得那看起来很像我丈夫的那杯“开往布鲁克林的F线特级苦味酒”？

1626
01:15:51.420 --> 01:15:52.660
Yes, I did, Angela.
对，我看到了，安吉拉。

1627
01:15:53.000 --> 01:15:54.300
Yeah, with the little toothpick?
对，还带着那个小牙签？

1628
01:15:54.360 --> 01:15:54.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1629
01:15:54.640 --> 01:15:55.200
The whole thing.
整杯都是。

1630
01:15:55.600 --> 01:15:57.080
We talked about this with BJ.
我们跟BJ讨论过这个。

1631
01:15:57.340 --> 01:15:59.500
All of the bachelorettes actually had a line.
所有的单身女郎其实都有一句台词。

1632
01:15:59.640 --> 01:16:02.700
It's in the extended cut on the DVD if you want to see the full scene.
如果你想看完整片段，DVD的加长版里有。

1633
01:16:02.700 --> 01:16:05.600
Yes, I've got a location alert.
是的，我有一个取景地提醒。

1634
01:16:05.920 --> 01:16:09.120
This location was the same as the funky cat.
这个取景地和那个时髦的猫咪酒吧是同一个。

1635
01:16:09.340 --> 01:16:11.580
We just used a different side of the bar.
我们只是用了酒吧的另一边。

1636
01:16:11.780 --> 01:16:12.680
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1637
01:16:12.860 --> 01:16:13.380
So smart.
太聪明了。

1638
01:16:13.600 --> 01:16:13.920
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1639
01:16:14.600 --> 01:16:20.040
Well, Karen is going to have a talking head saying, why did you single my line out like a million years later?
好吧，凯伦会有一段单人访谈，说“为什么过了一百万年之后你还要单独挑出我的台词”？

1640
01:16:20.280 --> 01:16:25.680
And at 13 minutes, four seconds, for my background folks, you will see another cameo callback.
而在13分04秒，对于关注背景的朋友们，你们会看到另一个客串彩蛋。

1641
01:16:26.120 --> 01:16:29.320
Dan Gore is exiting the cafe behind Karen's talking head.
丹·戈尔正从凯伦的单人访谈背景里的咖啡馆走出来。

1642
01:16:29.620 --> 01:16:31.640
You know, Dan played Karen's baby daddy.
你知道的，丹演的是凯伦孩子的爹。

1643
01:16:31.940 --> 01:16:32.380
Yes.
对。

1644
01:16:32.920 --> 01:16:37.240
Didn't he dress as a hot dog in a photo on her desk or something like that?
他是不是在凯伦桌上的一张照片里打扮成了一个热狗什么的？

1645
01:16:37.380 --> 01:16:38.080
That's amazing.
太绝了。

1646
01:16:38.580 --> 01:16:43.960
As the scene continues in the bar, we find out that Skarn is really depressed, you know?
随着酒吧里的场景继续，我们发现斯卡恩真的很沮丧，对吧？

1647
01:16:44.080 --> 01:16:45.560
And Billy is going to cheer him up.
然后比利要来让他振作起来。

1648
01:16:45.760 --> 01:16:48.880
He tells a random kid in overalls, who is this kid?
他跟一个穿工装裤的随机小孩说，这小孩是谁？

1649
01:16:49.940 --> 01:16:52.180
That kid was played by Joshua Reed.
那个小孩是由约书亚·里德饰演的。

1650
01:16:52.420 --> 01:16:54.420
All I could think of is like, is this a shroot?
我脑子里一直想的是，这难道是个施鲁特家族的人吗？

1651
01:16:54.660 --> 01:16:58.180
Like, is one of Dwight's nephews or cousins in town?
话说回来，德怀特的侄子还是表亲在镇上吗？

1652
01:16:58.180 --> 01:17:02.560
Anyway, he tells the little boy to hit G9 on the jukebox.
总之，他叫小男孩去点唱机上按G9。

1653
01:17:03.240 --> 01:17:05.080
It's time to dance the Skarn.
是时候跳斯坎舞了。

1654
01:17:05.300 --> 01:17:07.480
Oh, we talked about this with BJ.
哦，我们和BJ讨论过这个。

1655
01:17:07.880 --> 01:17:08.900
It was so fun.
太好玩了。

1656
01:17:09.060 --> 01:17:10.180
All you guys are so funny.
你们大家都好有趣。

1657
01:17:10.320 --> 01:17:12.360
I love all the cameos in the background of this scene.
我好喜欢这场戏背景里的所有客串。

1658
01:17:12.480 --> 01:17:13.580
We've got the whole warehouse.
整个仓库的人都在。

1659
01:17:13.580 --> 01:17:18.020
And then we have Leo from Vance Refrigeration, but not Gino.
然后我们还有范斯冷气的里奥，不过没有基诺。

1660
01:17:18.280 --> 01:17:22.140
I guess in real life, Gene was like, nah, I don't want to do the Skarn.
我猜在现实生活中，吉恩当时是说，算了，我才不想跳斯坎舞。

1661
01:17:22.180 --> 01:17:23.580
Well, Leo's having a good time.
好吧，里奥玩得很开心。

1662
01:17:23.620 --> 01:17:25.420
And we also have Todd Packer.
而且我们还有托德·帕克。

1663
01:17:25.420 --> 01:17:25.900
Yeah.
对啊。

1664
01:17:26.500 --> 01:17:29.480
I will tell you, the day we filmed this was such a blaSt.
我得告诉你们，我们拍这一天的时候可太开心了。

1665
01:17:29.660 --> 01:17:33.600
We, of course, had to learn the dance and practice it a few times.
我们当然得学这支舞，还排练了好几次。

1666
01:17:34.180 --> 01:17:38.520
And we also had to figure out how our character would dance, how up for it they would be.
我们还得琢磨自己的角色会怎么跳，他们对这有多热衷。

1667
01:17:39.200 --> 01:17:41.780
And I just have such fond memories of this day.
对于这一天，我有着非常美好的回忆。

1668
01:17:42.300 --> 01:17:47.720
We had a fan question from Avery G in Idaho who asked, who choreographed the Skarn?
我们收到了来自爱达荷州艾弗里·G的粉丝提问，问是谁编排的斯坎舞？

1669
01:17:48.140 --> 01:17:52.400
Well, I'll tell you, first of all, the lyrics were by BJ and the music was by Eve Nelson again.
好吧，我来告诉你，首先，歌词是BJ写的，音乐依然是伊芙·纳尔逊创作的。

1670
01:17:52.400 --> 01:17:55.520
And the choreography was by Marianne Kellogg.
编舞则是玛丽安·凯洛格。

1671
01:17:55.960 --> 01:17:58.600
She's done all our choreography on the show, and she's great.
她包办了我们剧里所有的舞蹈编排，她太棒了。

1672
01:17:58.880 --> 01:18:00.360
Well, she was very patient with us.
嗯，她对我们真的很有耐心。

1673
01:18:00.480 --> 01:18:05.000
If you look at the group who learned the Skarn, we are all different levels of dance skill set.
如果你看看学斯坎舞的那群人，我们的舞蹈功底其实各不相同。

1674
01:18:05.540 --> 01:18:07.660
I mean, this is not a difficult dance, though.
我的意思是，不过这也不是一支多难的舞。

1675
01:18:07.800 --> 01:18:09.720
It's not, but we had to get the timing right.
确实不难，但我们得把节奏对准。

1676
01:18:09.880 --> 01:18:12.800
But we also had to make it look like we didn't over know it.
但我们还得表现得好像我们没那么熟练似的。

1677
01:18:13.140 --> 01:18:13.740
Do you know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

1678
01:18:13.840 --> 01:18:14.200
I do.
我懂。

1679
01:18:14.880 --> 01:18:18.220
Back in the conference room, the Skarn is giving Jim the giggles.
回到会议室，斯坎舞把吉姆逗得咯咯直笑。

1680
01:18:18.420 --> 01:18:19.640
He can't stop laughing.
他笑得停不下来。

1681
01:18:20.020 --> 01:18:21.340
Here's a tidbit for you.
这里有个小花絮告诉你们。

1682
01:18:21.340 --> 01:18:27.640
On the DVD, they said, we shot this conference room scene with everyone reacting on the first day.
在DVD里，他们说，这场每个人都有反应的会议室戏是在第一天拍的。

1683
01:18:27.900 --> 01:18:29.680
So nothing had been filmed yet.
所以当时什么都还没拍呢。

1684
01:18:29.880 --> 01:18:31.920
So John is laughing at nothing.
所以约翰其实是对着空气在笑。

1685
01:18:32.700 --> 01:18:38.540
Wait, so the entire time we cut back to the conference room, all of us are watching nothing?
等等，也就是说每次切回会议室的时候，我们所有人都在看着空气？

1686
01:18:38.760 --> 01:18:39.160
Nothing.
对着空气。

1687
01:18:39.900 --> 01:18:41.300
Can you believe that?
你敢相信吗？

1688
01:18:41.560 --> 01:18:44.020
I mean, I don't even remember it that way.
我的意思是，在我的记忆里根本不是这样的。

1689
01:18:44.200 --> 01:18:45.260
That's what's so crazy.
这才是最疯狂的地方。

1690
01:18:45.600 --> 01:18:46.580
I was there.
我当时明明在场。

1691
01:18:46.580 --> 01:18:54.160
BJ said, John, when he's having this laughing fit, is watching nothing, and he was amazed at how well it timed out.
BJ说，约翰发笑的时候，其实什么都没看，而他自己都惊讶于时间点竟然掐得这么准。

1692
01:18:54.500 --> 01:18:54.900
Wow.
哇。

1693
01:18:55.300 --> 01:19:01.500
Well, the laughing is going to really upset Michael, and so much so he's going to pause the movie and walk out.
好吧，这笑声彻底惹恼了迈克尔，以至于他要暂停电影直接走人。

1694
01:19:01.680 --> 01:19:01.900
Yep.
没错。

1695
01:19:02.180 --> 01:19:04.280
And everyone is like, no, no, no, the movie's great.
大家都在喊，不不不，这电影挺好的。

1696
01:19:04.460 --> 01:19:04.980
Don't leave.
别走啊。

1697
01:19:04.980 --> 01:19:10.080
And that's when Michael turns to Holly and says if she liked the movie, and she says, which part?
然后迈克尔转头问霍莉是不是觉得电影好看，而她说，哪一部分？

1698
01:19:10.700 --> 01:19:11.460
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1699
01:19:11.960 --> 01:19:12.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1700
01:19:12.280 --> 01:19:22.320
This leads to that scene in the annex that we talked all about with BJ, and Michael's talking head about ants versus a bug's life.
这就引出了我们和BJ聊过的那个在隔间里的场景，以及迈克尔关于《蚁哥正传》对比《虫虫危机》的单人访谈。

1701
01:19:22.480 --> 01:19:22.760
Yeah.
对。

1702
01:19:23.180 --> 01:19:30.340
And Michael, who is heartbroken that Holly does not understand how important this movie is to him, is going to watch the rest of the movie.
迈克尔因为霍莉不明白这部电影对他的重要性而心碎，他打算接着把电影看完。

1703
01:19:30.520 --> 01:19:31.100
Without her.
没有她。

1704
01:19:31.340 --> 01:19:31.600
Yeah.
对。

1705
01:19:32.000 --> 01:19:32.300
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1706
01:19:32.840 --> 01:19:38.520
But as he watches it without her, he starts to sort of see it through her filter, right?
但当他没有她陪着看的时候，他开始有点用她的视角来看待这部电影，对吧？

1707
01:19:38.780 --> 01:19:39.160
Yeah.
对。

1708
01:19:39.160 --> 01:19:45.000
And as he's looking at her empty seat, he then looks out the conference room window, and there she is.
当他看着她空着座位时，他望向了会议室的窗外，结果她就在那儿。

1709
01:19:45.100 --> 01:19:45.980
She's watching it.
她在看着。

1710
01:19:46.120 --> 01:19:47.520
He runs out to her.
他跑出去找她。

1711
01:19:47.820 --> 01:19:49.160
He apologizes.
他道歉了。

1712
01:19:49.320 --> 01:19:50.380
She apologizes.
她也道歉了。

1713
01:19:50.880 --> 01:19:51.740
They kiss.
他们接吻了。

1714
01:19:51.880 --> 01:19:53.340
They go back in to watch it together.
他们又回去一起看了。

1715
01:19:53.540 --> 01:19:54.700
They're such a good couple.
他们真的是很好的一对。

1716
01:19:54.700 --> 01:19:55.600
They really are.
确实是。

1717
01:19:55.840 --> 01:19:59.140
She gets him, and she's making him a better person.
她懂他，而且她正在让他变得更好。

1718
01:19:59.400 --> 01:19:59.840
Yes.
对。

1719
01:20:00.120 --> 01:20:00.540
Yes.
没错。

1720
01:20:00.540 --> 01:20:04.940
I think that was the whole point of this plot, was to mature Michael.
我觉得这个情节的全部意义，就是为了让迈克尔变得成熟。

1721
01:20:05.180 --> 01:20:05.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1722
01:20:05.900 --> 01:20:09.000
Lady, we had a fan question from Paige M in Philly.
各位，我们收到了来自费城的粉丝佩吉·M的提问。

1723
01:20:09.160 --> 01:20:15.020
Paige asks, when everyone is watching Threat Level Midnight for the second time, Michael gets up to check on Holly.
佩吉问，当大家第二次观看《零点危机》时，迈克尔起身去查看霍莉的情况。

1724
01:20:15.340 --> 01:20:20.280
At that time, Golden Face is telling Pam why his face is gold.
当时，金面人正在告诉帕姆为什么他的脸是金色的。

1725
01:20:20.460 --> 01:20:25.460
However, the audience misses it because we are listening to Michael and Holly's conversation.
然而，观众们错过了这段，因为我们在听迈克尔和霍莉的对话。

1726
01:20:25.780 --> 01:20:28.540
I want to know, what was he saying?
我想知道，他当时在说什么？

1727
01:20:29.180 --> 01:20:35.600
I actually found this scene in the shooting draft, but it's also in the extended movie on the DVD as well.
我其实在拍摄剧本里找到了这一幕，不过DVD的加长版电影里也有。

1728
01:20:35.940 --> 01:20:39.420
I'm going to set it up from the shooting draft, and then I'm going to play the clip.
我先根据拍摄剧本做个铺垫，然后播放这段音频。

1729
01:20:39.720 --> 01:20:40.000
Great.
太好了。

1730
01:20:40.520 --> 01:20:43.080
The script said, interior stadium warehouse.
剧本上写着，内景，体育场仓库。

1731
01:20:43.460 --> 01:20:44.940
The hostages are scared.
人质们很害怕。

1732
01:20:45.220 --> 01:20:46.200
Kevin is praying.
凯文在祈祷。

1733
01:20:47.020 --> 01:20:49.220
Roy says to Pam, now's your chance.
罗伊对帕姆说，现在是你的机会了。

1734
01:20:49.420 --> 01:20:50.500
Go talk to Golden Face.
去跟金面人谈谈。

1735
01:20:50.880 --> 01:20:51.800
See what you can do.
看看你能做点什么。

1736
01:20:52.260 --> 01:20:57.940
Pam approaches Golden Face, and in the script it says that Pam's character is flirtatious.
帕姆走向金面人，剧本里写着帕姆的角色带点调情意味。

1737
01:20:58.200 --> 01:20:58.480
Oh.
哦。

1738
01:20:58.860 --> 01:20:59.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1739
01:20:59.960 --> 01:21:01.760
So Pam had some stage direction.
所以帕姆有一些舞台提示。

1740
01:21:02.320 --> 01:21:03.680
Let's hear the rest of it.
我们听听剩下的部分。

1741
01:21:04.200 --> 01:21:05.020
Now's your chance.
现在是你的机会了。

1742
01:21:05.540 --> 01:21:06.680
Go talk to Golden Face.
去跟金面人谈谈。

1743
01:21:07.140 --> 01:21:08.340
See what you can do.
看看你能做点什么。

1744
01:21:08.940 --> 01:21:09.300
Okay.
好吧。

1745
01:21:10.760 --> 01:21:12.000
Hey, Golden Face.
嘿，金面人。

1746
01:21:12.660 --> 01:21:14.180
Can I ask you a question?
我能问你个问题吗？

1747
01:21:15.260 --> 01:21:20.920
I mean, since we're all going to die here anyway, why is your face gold?
我的意思是，反正我们横竖都要死在这儿，为什么你的脸是金色的？

1748
01:21:21.240 --> 01:21:22.220
Why do you care?
关你什么事？

1749
01:21:22.500 --> 01:21:23.960
I'm just making conversation.
我只是随便聊聊。

1750
01:21:24.560 --> 01:21:26.140
I worked in a gold factory.
我在一家黄金工厂工作过。

1751
01:21:26.580 --> 01:21:29.200
We had a boss who only cared about money.
我们以前有个老板，眼里只有钱。

1752
01:21:30.260 --> 01:21:34.860
He wouldn't give us lunch break, so we had to eat the gold.
他连午休都不给我们，所以我们只好吃黄金。

1753
01:21:35.480 --> 01:21:44.520
And then one day, I looked in the mirror, and, well, I guess you are what you eat.
然后有一天，我照了照镜子，然后，嗯，我想人如其食吧。

1754
01:21:45.200 --> 01:21:47.960
Golden Face, that is so sad.
黄金脸，这太令人难过了。

1755
01:21:48.420 --> 01:21:54.220
Well, I just thought if I could blow up all the All-Star games, all the trophies would explode all over the place,
嗯，我只是觉得如果我能炸毁所有全明星赛，所有的奖杯就会到处爆炸，

1756
01:21:54.220 --> 01:21:57.940
and then everyone would be gold, just like me.
然后每个人都会变成金色，就像我一样。

1757
01:21:59.990 --> 01:22:02.010
Please let us go, Golden Face.
请放我们走吧，黄金脸。

1758
01:22:02.170 --> 01:22:03.050
So sad.
太难过了。

1759
01:22:06.740 --> 01:22:17.500
You know, what you can't see when you play that clip is that at the end of that scene, Sandra, played by Pam, gives Golden Face a kiss on his cheek.
你知道的，你播那段视频时看不到的是，在那场戏结束时，由潘扮演的桑德拉在黄金脸的脸颊上亲了一下。

1760
01:22:17.500 --> 01:22:26.040
Yeah, and in the shooting draft, it said, after the scene plays, you cut back to real time in the conference room,
对啊，在拍摄剧本里写着，这段戏演完后，镜头切回会议室的现实时间，

1761
01:22:26.160 --> 01:22:31.360
and Jim and Pam are holding hands, enjoying the scene, remembering what that meant to them.
吉姆和潘手拉着手，欣赏着这一幕，回忆着这对他们的意义。

1762
01:22:31.520 --> 01:22:35.560
I mean, Pam got to kiss Jim's cheek in front of Roy.
我是说，潘竟然当着罗伊的面亲了吉姆的脸颊。

1763
01:22:35.560 --> 01:22:36.520
I know.
我知道。

1764
01:22:37.180 --> 01:22:37.620
Wow.
哇。

1765
01:22:38.100 --> 01:22:42.200
Back in the movie, Michael Skarn has taken to the ice.
回到电影里，迈克尔·斯坎恩已经上了冰场。

1766
01:22:42.600 --> 01:22:47.240
I really love the detail that Michael tells us in the conference room,
我真的很喜欢迈克尔在会议室里告诉我们的细节，

1767
01:22:47.280 --> 01:22:52.740
which is that he filmed this during an actual Scranton high school hockey game,
那就是他是斯克兰顿高中一场真正的曲棍球比赛期间拍摄的，

1768
01:22:52.740 --> 01:22:55.980
and that it was kind of a big deal because they were trying to qualify,
这其实是一件大事，因为他们当时正试图获得晋级资格，

1769
01:22:56.640 --> 01:23:00.580
and then the team got disqualified because Michael messed things up.
然后因为迈克尔把事情搞砸了，这支球队就被取消了资格。

1770
01:23:00.580 --> 01:23:05.800
He ruined all of their dreams of, like, going on and winning a championship.
他毁了他们所有人继续前进并赢得冠军的梦想。

1771
01:23:05.860 --> 01:23:08.660
They had had an undefeated season up until now.
在此之前，他们整个赛季保持不败。

1772
01:23:08.840 --> 01:23:09.080
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

1773
01:23:09.220 --> 01:23:13.200
And they were disqualified because this idiot took to the ice to film his movie.
而且他们被取消资格，就是因为这个白痴为了拍电影跑上了冰场。

1774
01:23:13.500 --> 01:23:18.280
Well, the actual location of this shoot was at the Valencia Ice Station,
好吧，这次拍摄的实际地点是在巴伦西亚滑冰场，

1775
01:23:18.280 --> 01:23:22.380
and all of those people were extras that we hired, of course.
当然，所有那些人都是我们雇的群众演员。

1776
01:23:22.380 --> 01:23:23.680
It was a big production.
这是一次大制作。

1777
01:23:23.900 --> 01:23:24.620
It really was.
确实如此。

1778
01:23:25.060 --> 01:23:28.260
Cherokee Jack is going to visit Skarn from the dead?
切罗基·杰克要从阴间来看望斯坎恩？

1779
01:23:28.420 --> 01:23:29.420
Is he a ghost?
他是鬼吗？

1780
01:23:29.660 --> 01:23:29.920
Yeah.
对。

1781
01:23:30.140 --> 01:23:30.320
Yeah.
对。

1782
01:23:30.520 --> 01:23:35.000
And he's going to tell Skarn to take out all of his frustrations on that hockey puck.
然后他要告诉斯坎恩把所有的郁闷都发泄在那个冰球上。

1783
01:23:35.720 --> 01:23:39.460
And Skarn hits it so hard that it flies into space.
然后斯坎恩用力一击，冰球飞进了太空。

1784
01:23:39.840 --> 01:23:41.320
It hits a satellite.
它击中了卫星。

1785
01:23:41.540 --> 01:23:41.760
Yeah.
对。

1786
01:23:41.920 --> 01:23:43.780
All of a sudden, Billy's TV works again.
突然之间，比利家的电视又能用了。

1787
01:23:44.420 --> 01:23:49.140
And then it eventually lands in the lap of Golden Face,
然后它最后落在了黄金脸的腿上，

1788
01:23:49.140 --> 01:23:54.580
who's sitting in his backyard counting a suitcase full of money.
他正坐在后院里数着一整手提箱的钱。

1789
01:23:54.780 --> 01:23:57.840
Yeah, he's in a lawn chair counting money.
对，他坐在躺椅上数钱。

1790
01:23:58.100 --> 01:23:59.900
Where did the money come from?
钱是从哪里来的？

1791
01:24:00.100 --> 01:24:00.840
I don't know.
我不知道。

1792
01:24:01.000 --> 01:24:02.540
But he goes, oh, s***.
但他来了句，哦，靠。

1793
01:24:02.920 --> 01:24:05.580
Oh, standards and practices lady.
哦，审查部门的女士。

1794
01:24:05.960 --> 01:24:08.380
Here were the notes from standards and practices.
以下是审查部门的意见。

1795
01:24:09.180 --> 01:24:13.720
Scene 86, please lose the underlined.
第86场，请去掉下划线。

1796
01:24:14.540 --> 01:24:20.560
Or have the explosion start sooner when we see the puck land on Golden Face's lap,
或者当看到冰球落在黄金脸腿上时，让爆炸开始得更早一点，

1797
01:24:20.580 --> 01:24:23.140
and he says, oh, shh.
然后他说，哦，靠。

1798
01:24:23.280 --> 01:24:25.420
And they underlined the shh.
而他们给“靠”字加了下划线。

1799
01:24:25.820 --> 01:24:29.620
Somebody was like, listen, they're not going to take us seriously unless you underline it.
有人就像是，听着，除非你加上下划线，否则他们不会把我们当回事。

1800
01:24:29.840 --> 01:24:30.840
It's in bold.
这还是加粗的。

1801
01:24:31.120 --> 01:24:31.500
You know what?
你知道吗？

1802
01:24:31.500 --> 01:24:32.540
They put it in bold, too.
他们还用了加粗。

1803
01:24:32.720 --> 01:24:33.440
Here's my other note.
这是我的另一条笔记。

1804
01:24:33.560 --> 01:24:34.080
Make it bold.
把它加粗。

1805
01:24:34.200 --> 01:24:34.660
Underline it.
画上下划线。

1806
01:24:34.720 --> 01:24:35.420
Do you have a highlighter?
你有荧光笔吗？

1807
01:24:35.560 --> 01:24:36.080
Highlight it.
把它高亮标记。

1808
01:24:36.080 --> 01:24:37.400
Put an arrow by it.
旁边画个箭头。

1809
01:24:37.580 --> 01:24:41.860
So that's why we can see John's mouth go into the shh.
所以这就是为什么我们能看到约翰的嘴做出嘘声的动作。

1810
01:24:41.960 --> 01:24:44.840
We were allowed that silent lip flap,
我们允许那种无声的嘴唇开合，

1811
01:24:44.900 --> 01:24:49.960
but the explosion had to go off before we heard him make the sound.
但爆炸必须在我们听到他发出声音之前发生。

1812
01:24:50.200 --> 01:24:51.100
Underline it.
画上下划线。

1813
01:24:51.700 --> 01:24:52.300
Exactly.
完全正确。

1814
01:24:52.720 --> 01:24:57.180
Well, the location of this scene was our very own Tom Milby's backyard.
嗯，这个场景的取景地就是我们自己的汤姆·米尔比的后院。

1815
01:24:57.400 --> 01:24:58.680
I recognized it immediately.
我一眼就认出来了。

1816
01:24:58.980 --> 01:24:59.800
Me too, right away.
我也是，马上就认出来了。

1817
01:25:00.500 --> 01:25:04.320
He lived in a house right behind our stages.
他住的房子就在我们片场后面。

1818
01:25:04.620 --> 01:25:05.800
Yeah, we've talked about it.
对，我们聊过这个。

1819
01:25:05.800 --> 01:25:08.640
He had a little swing, and I'd walk over there with Isabel on my lunch.
他有个小秋千，我午休时会带着伊莎贝尔走过去。

1820
01:25:08.880 --> 01:25:10.480
Well, everyone cheers.
好吧，大家都欢呼起来。

1821
01:25:10.820 --> 01:25:12.520
Scarn has saved the day.
斯卡恩拯救了世界。

1822
01:25:13.100 --> 01:25:14.020
It's amazing.
太惊艳了。

1823
01:25:14.160 --> 01:25:15.800
He's back at his house.
他回到了自己的家中。

1824
01:25:16.100 --> 01:25:17.660
He's having breakfaSt.
他正在吃早餐。

1825
01:25:18.840 --> 01:25:21.100
And the president calls again.
然后总统又打电话来了。

1826
01:25:21.820 --> 01:25:24.360
He has another mission for Scarn.
他给斯卡恩派了另一个任务。

1827
01:25:24.840 --> 01:25:26.500
Should he choose to accept?
他会选择接受吗？

1828
01:25:26.940 --> 01:25:28.220
Also, one side note.
另外，还有一个题外话。

1829
01:25:28.400 --> 01:25:28.800
Yes.
对。

1830
01:25:28.940 --> 01:25:31.140
He realizes, oh, yeah, he did make Dwight a robot.
他意识到，哦，对了，他确实把德怀特变成了一个机器人。

1831
01:25:31.140 --> 01:25:34.680
Yes, because there is a scene of him oiling his circuit board.
对，因为有一个场景是他给德怀特的电路板上油。

1832
01:25:35.080 --> 01:25:41.820
And as the movie comes to an end, the narrator, it's been Stanley's voice this whole time.
随着电影接近尾声，旁白，其实一直都是斯坦利的的声音。

1833
01:25:42.080 --> 01:25:43.180
Plot twiSt.
剧情大反转。

1834
01:25:43.460 --> 01:25:46.720
That voice is coming out of Michael Scarn.
那个声音是从迈克尔·斯卡恩口中发出的。

1835
01:25:47.440 --> 01:25:49.140
He is Michael Scarn.
他就是迈克尔·斯卡恩。

1836
01:25:50.220 --> 01:25:52.360
He's been narrating his own story.
他一直在叙述他自己的故事。

1837
01:25:52.540 --> 01:25:53.140
The whole time.
自始至终。

1838
01:25:53.580 --> 01:25:56.260
The Office erupts in cheers.
办公室里爆发出一阵欢呼。

1839
01:25:56.380 --> 01:25:57.740
It's a huge hit.
这是一部巨大的热门作品。

1840
01:25:58.140 --> 01:26:00.320
Everybody loved Threat Level Midnight.
每个人都喜欢《威胁级别：午夜》。

1841
01:26:00.620 --> 01:26:00.940
Yeah.
对。

1842
01:26:00.940 --> 01:26:03.000
It was a pretty fun day at The Office.
在办公室里那是相当有趣的一天。

1843
01:26:03.500 --> 01:26:09.900
You know, the episode ends with the sort of end credits for the movie.
你知道，这一集以电影的类似片尾字幕结束。

1844
01:26:09.900 --> 01:26:13.280
And the theme song of Threat Level Midnight that we talked about with BJ.
还有我们跟BJ聊过的《威胁级别：午夜》的主题曲。

1845
01:26:13.580 --> 01:26:15.880
I thought it was really cute on the DVD.
我觉得DVD上的这个设计真的很可爱。

1846
01:26:16.400 --> 01:26:18.500
This is how that song is credited.
这首歌的署名是这样的。

1847
01:26:18.960 --> 01:26:19.800
It says,
上面写着，

1848
01:26:20.020 --> 01:26:21.720
Theme from Threat Level Midnight.
《威胁级别：午夜》主题曲。

1849
01:26:21.920 --> 01:26:23.720
Music and lyrics by Michael Scott.
词曲作者：迈克尔·斯科特。

1850
01:26:23.940 --> 01:26:25.360
Performed by Andrew Bernard.
演唱：安迪·伯纳德。

1851
01:26:25.880 --> 01:26:27.720
Inspired by the music of Will Smith.
灵感源自威尔·史密斯的音乐。

1852
01:26:28.620 --> 01:26:32.440
I just love when Michael always gives credit to who inspired him.
我特别喜欢迈克尔总是向启发他的人致谢。

1853
01:26:33.180 --> 01:26:37.820
Well, on the DVD, BJ and Charlie talked about this final rap at the end.
对，在DVD里，BJ和查理谈到了最后这段说唱。

1854
01:26:38.000 --> 01:26:39.800
And Charlie wrote it.
而且是查理写的。

1855
01:26:39.880 --> 01:26:44.100
And BJ said he remembered that Charlie wrote it in what seemed to be like five minutes.
BJ说他记得查理写这个好像只用了五分钟左右。

1856
01:26:44.460 --> 01:26:45.900
It just flowed.
一气呵成。

1857
01:26:46.080 --> 01:26:46.200
Yeah.
没错。

1858
01:26:47.060 --> 01:26:56.860
Well, at the end of the credits, there was going to be an additional tag of Dwight as Samuel coming in and telling you to go home.
对，在职员表最后，本来还有一个额外的彩蛋，是德怀特扮演的塞缪尔走出来叫大家回家。

1859
01:26:57.020 --> 01:26:57.740
Go home.
回家吧。

1860
01:26:57.820 --> 01:26:58.580
The movie's over.
电影结束了。

1861
01:26:58.580 --> 01:27:00.040
Like at the end of Ferris Bueller.
就像《春天不是读书天》结尾那样。

1862
01:27:00.280 --> 01:27:00.500
Yeah.
对。

1863
01:27:00.680 --> 01:27:01.760
But we didn't have time.
不过我们当时没时间拍。

1864
01:27:02.180 --> 01:27:03.320
It's really cute, though.
不过真的挺可爱的。

1865
01:27:03.460 --> 01:27:04.540
It's in the extended cut.
加长版里有收录。

1866
01:27:04.860 --> 01:27:07.160
Well, that was our breakdown of Threat Level Midnight.
好了，以上就是我们对《威胁级午夜》的剖析。

1867
01:27:07.260 --> 01:27:09.980
But I do have one more little tidbit to share, Angela.
不过安吉拉，我还有一个小八卦要分享。

1868
01:27:10.260 --> 01:27:10.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1869
01:27:10.940 --> 01:27:14.940
Last year, there was a band called The Network who appeared on The Tonight Show.
去年，有一支名叫“网络”的乐队上了《今夜秀》。

1870
01:27:14.980 --> 01:27:19.480
And they performed a song called Threat Level Midnight.
他们表演了一首名为《威胁级午夜》的歌。

1871
01:27:19.640 --> 01:27:20.120
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

1872
01:27:20.440 --> 01:27:23.320
The Network is a new wave band.
“网络”是一支新浪潮乐队。

1873
01:27:23.440 --> 01:27:28.120
But they are a side project of the rock band Green Day.
但他们是摇滚乐队“绿日”的副业项目。

1874
01:27:28.580 --> 01:27:31.060
Oh, Billy Joe, our best friend.
哦，比利·乔，我们最好的朋友。

1875
01:27:31.060 --> 01:27:32.200
And your best friend.
也是你最好的朋友。

1876
01:27:32.360 --> 01:27:33.360
I'm kind of glomming on now.
我这会儿正厚着脸皮往上凑呢。

1877
01:27:33.700 --> 01:27:34.740
You hung out.
你们一起玩过。

1878
01:27:34.900 --> 01:27:35.580
I met him.
我见了他。

1879
01:27:35.700 --> 01:27:36.220
We hung out.
我们一起聚过。

1880
01:27:36.340 --> 01:27:38.180
We had a really nice conversation.
我们聊得很开心。

1881
01:27:38.420 --> 01:27:40.980
The three of us are basically best friends now, Angela.
安吉拉，我们三个现在基本上是最好的朋友了。

1882
01:27:41.180 --> 01:27:41.700
In your mind.
那是你以为的。

1883
01:27:41.820 --> 01:27:43.420
We have a photo to prove it.
我们有照片为证。

1884
01:27:43.820 --> 01:27:47.900
We'll put it in stories because I'm dying to prove our friendship.
我们会把它发到快拍里，因为我急于证明我们的友谊。

1885
01:27:48.580 --> 01:27:51.140
But anyway, it's a really fun song.
不管怎样，这是一首非常好玩的歌。

1886
01:27:51.280 --> 01:27:57.060
And actually, when they went to release this, Billy Joe texted me this song out of nowhere
事实上，当他们准备发行这首歌时，比利·乔突然给我发了这首歌的短信

1887
01:27:57.060 --> 01:27:58.320
with no context.
什么前情提要都没有。

1888
01:27:58.580 --> 01:28:00.900
I didn't even know he had started watching The Office yet.
我甚至不知道他已经开始看《办公室》了。

1889
01:28:01.140 --> 01:28:02.260
It's really catchy.
真的很洗脑。

1890
01:28:02.680 --> 01:28:04.640
And my family listens to it all the time.
我的家人经常听。

1891
01:28:04.640 --> 01:28:08.000
So I thought maybe we could end this episode by playing it.
所以我想也许我们可以在这集结尾时放这首歌。

1892
01:28:08.160 --> 01:28:09.140
Let's hear it.
我们听听看。

1893
01:28:09.400 --> 01:28:11.280
Threat Level Midnight by The Network.
《威胁级午夜》，由“网络”乐队演唱。

1894
01:28:11.760 --> 01:28:11.940
Yes.
好的。

1895
01:28:11.940 --> 01:28:35.390
Threat Level Midnight, a big thank you to BJ Novak for joining us today.
《威胁级午夜》，非常感谢BJ·诺瓦克今天加入我们。

1896
01:28:35.650 --> 01:28:38.730
Yes, and Randy Cordray for all the behind-the-scenes details.
对，还有兰迪·科德雷分享的所有幕后细节。

1897
01:28:38.730 --> 01:28:41.830
And you guys for sending in your questions and comments.
还有感谢你们发来提问和评论。

1898
01:28:42.050 --> 01:28:43.150
Thanks so much.
非常感谢。

1899
01:28:43.330 --> 01:28:44.350
See you next week.
下周见。

1900
01:28:44.350 --> 01:28:54.230
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1901
01:28:54.530 --> 01:28:58.430
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由 Earwolf、珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金西联合制作。

1902
01:28:58.710 --> 01:29:01.370
Our show is executive produced by Cody Fisher.
我们的节目执行制片人是科迪·费舍。

1903
01:29:01.630 --> 01:29:03.770
Our producer is Cassie Jerkins.
我们的制片人是卡西·杰金斯。

1904
01:29:03.930 --> 01:29:05.750
Our sound engineer is Sam Kiefer.
我们的录音师是萨姆·基弗。

1905
01:29:05.990 --> 01:29:08.270
And our associate producer is Ainsley Bubba Coe.
我们的副制片人是艾因斯利·布巴·科e。

1906
01:29:08.510 --> 01:29:11.350
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是由克里德·布拉顿演唱的《橡胶树》。

1907
